NAME

ulibFileSubDir - Returns the name of a file section subdirectory


SYNOPSIS

UBYTE *ulibFileSubDir(long Section, long SubDir)
                           d0           d1

DESCRIPTION

This function returns the path of subdirectory number <SubDir> of file section
<Section>, where <SubDir> is zero (0) for the first subdirectory, one (1) for
the second, etc.


RETURNS

This function will return NULL if an invalid subdirectory number is requested
(i.e. one that does not exist in the configuration), or a pointer to the
subdirectory name if the operation was successful.


SEE ALSO

